# Component tsx

For part/main files (not `context/**`, not `*.test.tsx`):

- Bind with `useRender` + `mergeProps`.
- Call `applyA11y` / `applyAttrs` once; do not re-list N params into old-style helpers.
- Component prop order: `ref`, `render`, custom, native, `disabled`, `className`, `children`, `...props`.
- `useRender({…})` key order: `defaultTagName`, `ref`, `render`, `state`, `enabled`, `props` (omit unused).
- `mergeProps` bag order (later wins — JS/`mergeProps` behavior): owned bag → `applyA11y` / `applyAttrs` → `props` → optional locks that must beat rest (e.g. `{ disabled }` when the component MD says so). Do not invent locks without an MD contract.
